import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — gate 3: parametric abstraction over the step (a measured FAIL, deeper than the last)","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — gate 3: parametric abstraction over the step (a measured FAIL, deeper than the last)","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/gate3-parametric-abstraction.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/gate3-parametric-abstraction.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/gate3-parametric-abstraction.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-gate-3-parametric-abstraction-over-the-step-a-measured-fail-deeper-than-the-last" tabindex="-1">Retro — gate 3: parametric abstraction over the step (a measured FAIL, deeper than the last) <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-gate-3-parametric-abstraction-over-the-step-a-measured-fail-deeper-than-the-last" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — gate 3: parametric abstraction over the step (a measured FAIL, deeper than the last)”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Commit</strong>: <code>e4a193a</code> (catopt <code>main</code>). <strong>Decides</strong>: ADR 0008 gate 3 → still <strong>FAIL</strong>, now with the <em>cause</em> measured; ADR 0009 stage 4 stays unjustified on this evidence.</p><h2 id="what-the-gate-was-and-what-was-missing" tabindex="-1">What the gate was, and what was missing <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-the-gate-was-and-what-was-missing" aria-label="Permalink to “What the gate was, and what was missing”">​</a></h2><p>The gate-3 retro (<code>gate3-loop-proposing-rule.md</code>) recorded that the <code>unroll(step, n) → Loop(step, n)</code> proposing rule works (control PASS) but fires <strong>0×</strong> on the search&#39;s winner, because the export&#39;s unrolled recurrence is <em>parametrically</em> regular (each block&#39;s step differs by the block index, <code>split(…, index=i)</code>) but not <em>syntactically</em> regular — there is no shared <code>step</code> subterm to bind. It named the missing piece: <strong>abstraction over the step</strong> — a form-level / parametric move, not an e-graph rewrite.</p><p>This task built that move and re-ran the protocol.</p><h2 id="what-was-built" tabindex="-1">What was built <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-was-built" aria-label="Permalink to “What was built”">​</a></h2><p><code>lab/bridge/index_abstract.py</code> (+ the <code>--abstract-index</code> arm in <code>lab/bridge/combinator_probe.py</code>; 12 tests in <code>tests/test_index_abstract.py</code>).</p><p>The move operates on the term&#39;s <strong>per-block decomposition</strong> — the leaves of the <code>concat</code> chain a chunked scan&#39;s output is — and does four things:</p><ol><li><strong>Decompose</strong> — flatten the <code>concat</code> chain into the <code>K</code> block outputs; find the <code>split(…, index=i)</code> families.</li><li><strong>Abstract the index</strong> — in each block, replace its <em>own</em> indexed <code>split</code> with a fresh <strong>block-input parameter</strong> (a wire). The index is no longer a baked constant.</li><li><strong>Abstract the state</strong> — replace the block&#39;s <strong>recurrence state</strong> (the outermost shared subterm that carries none of the block&#39;s own splits) with a fresh <strong>state parameter</strong>. The state is no longer a baked subterm.</li><li><strong>Test regularity, then fold</strong> — if all <code>K</code> abstracted templates are the <em>same</em> term, compile the shared template to a step morphism <code>S ⊗ X → S&#39; ⊗ Y</code> and emit <code>unroll(step, K)</code> (the spelling <code>PROPOSE_LOOP</code> folds to <code>Loop(step, K)</code>); otherwise report the <em>first</em> structural difference, so the negative names its own cause.</li></ol><p><strong>Vocabulary</strong>: only <code>split</code>/<code>Arr</code>/<code>Leaf</code>/<code>Loop</code> — the abstraction binds a constant as a <strong>parameter wire</strong>, so <strong>no new IR node kind</strong> is needed. That answers the brief&#39;s &quot;do not invent a node kind unless it is necessary&quot;: a parameter is just a wire, and the presentation already has wires and the <code>Loop</code> combinator.</p><p>The verdict requires <em>both</em> that the templates collapse <strong>and</strong> that the fold reproduces the original blocks (<code>roundtrip</code>). Templates agreeing is necessary but not sufficient — a family can collapse onto the wrong subterm and then fail to reproduce; that case is reported <code>irregular</code> (see the <code>old_linear</code> control below), never as a false pass.</p><h2 id="the-commands-and-the-numbers" tabindex="-1">The commands and the numbers <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-commands-and-the-numbers" aria-label="Permalink to “The commands and the numbers”">​</a></h2><div class="language-sh"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#62687b;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">#</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#BBBBBB;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#62687b;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;"> gate 3, unchanged protocol, both gate-3 arms armed</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;">.venv/bin/python</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#032F62;"> lab/bridge/combinator_probe.py</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#005CC5;"> \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#005CC5;">    --gate2</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#005CC5;"> --extracted</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#005CC5;"> --propose-loop</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#005CC5;"> --abstract-index</span></span></code></pre></div><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>-- projection (staged arm, T=64 K=4, 15s, 9755 enodes) --</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>   extracted term: dag=139  reads=2 chained=True</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>   projects: round-trip EQUAL  morph=1590 dup=92 copies=184</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>   fold-chain depth: spelled=3  extract=2</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>   the presentation&#39;s spelled scan is in the search&#39;s root e-class: False</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>-- gate 3: the \`loop\`-proposing rule --</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>   loop-propose: winner morph=1590 spelled-scan subterms (n&gt;=2) found=0 ns=[]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>      saturation: terms=1 fired={&#39;loop_propose&#39;: 0, &#39;loop_expand&#39;: 0}  loop-headed reachable=False  best_is_loop=False  best_cost=1590</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>   control (authored spelled scan): spelled-scan subterms=1 ns=[4] fired={&#39;loop_propose&#39;: 1, &#39;loop_expand&#39;: 0}  loop-headed reachable=True  best_is_loop=True  best_cost=69 (spelled 285)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>-- gate 3: parametric abstraction over the step --</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>   abstract-index: blocks=7 split-families=2</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>      family sizes/dim=(&#39;(16, 16, 16, 16)&#39;, -2) indices=[0, 1, 2, 3]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>      family sizes/dim=(&#39;(4, 4, 4, 4, 16, 16, 16)&#39;, -2) indices=[0, 1, 2, 3]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>      verdict=IRREGULAR — the 7 blocks do NOT collapse to one shared step</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>      first difference: block1/block2/add[1]/mul[1]: op om_decayed vs add</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>   control (regular fold): blocks=4 verdict=regular round-trip=True  closure: best_is_loop=True best_cost=109</span></span></code></pre></div><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>seed</th><th>blocks</th><th>abstraction verdict</th><th>fold round-trips</th><th>closure</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>winner</strong> (the gate)</td><td>7</td><td><strong>IRREGULAR</strong></td><td>— (no fold built)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>control — the <em>presentation&#39;s spelled fold</em>, expanded</td><td>4</td><td>regular</td><td><strong>True</strong></td><td><code>best_is_loop=True</code>, best_cost 109</td></tr><tr><td>synthetic <code>new</code> / <code>old_shielded</code> folds</td><td>4</td><td>regular</td><td>True</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>synthetic <code>old_linear</code> fold</td><td>4</td><td>irregular (agrees, does not reproduce)</td><td>False</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The control is the presentation&#39;s own spelled scan expanded (<code>_expanded_fold_term(t, k)</code>) — the gate-2 program, a genuine regular fold. The move collapses it to one shared step, round-trips, and the closure reaches a <code>Loop</code> (<code>best_is_loop=True</code>). Measured at <code>K = 2, 4, 8</code> (<code>T = 8, 64, 128</code>): <strong>regular + round-trip in all three</strong>.</p><h2 id="verdict-—-fail-against-the-adr-s-criterion" tabindex="-1">Verdict — FAIL, against the ADR&#39;s criterion <a class="header-anchor" href="#verdict-—-fail-against-the-adr-s-criterion" aria-label="Permalink to “Verdict — FAIL, against the ADR&#39;s criterion”">​</a></h2><blockquote><p><strong>FAIL</strong> = the winner is the spelled/unrolled form again → search did not reach <code>loop</code>.</p></blockquote><p>The winner does <strong>not</strong> collapse. The parametric abstraction — the move the previous retro named — cannot make its <code>K</code> blocks one shared <code>step</code>, and the move reports the first difference itself:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>block1/block2/add[1]/mul[1]: op om_decayed vs add</span></span></code></pre></div><p>i.e. at the <strong>cross-term position</strong> of the block, block 1 spells the state contribution as <code>om_decayed(matmul(q, k_prevᵀ), D, v_prev)</code> (a re-expansion of the state through the intra carrier) while block 2 spells it as an additive nesting. The blocks are not the same step modulo any constant.</p><h2 id="why-—-and-why-it-is-deeper-than-the-last-retro-s-diagnosis" tabindex="-1">Why — and why it is <em>deeper</em> than the last retro&#39;s diagnosis <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-—-and-why-it-is-deeper-than-the-last-retro-s-diagnosis" aria-label="Permalink to “Why — and why it is deeper than the last retro&#39;s diagnosis”">​</a></h2><p>The last retro blamed the split index alone (&quot;each block&#39;s step differs by <code>split(…, index=i)</code>&quot;). The abstraction <strong>removes the index</strong> and the blocks still do not agree, so the index was not the whole story. Measured on the winner&#39;s 139-node DAG:</p><ol><li><strong>The chunking is not uniform.</strong> The output is a <code>concat</code> of <strong>7</strong> blocks of <strong>two</strong> sizes — four of size 4 and three of size 16 (4·4 + 3·16 = 64) — drawn from <strong>two</strong> <code>split</code> families (<code>sizes=(4,4,4,4,16,16,16)</code> and <code>sizes=(16,16,16,16)</code>). The step&#39;s own <code>t</code>/<code>sizes</code> attrs differ across blocks; a <code>Loop</code> has one step shape.</li><li><strong>The state spelling is non-uniform.</strong> Extraction mixed two ways of reading the recurrence state: the <em>shared-state read</em> <code>matmul(q, S)</code> and the <em>intra re-expansion</em> <code>om_decayed(matmul(q, k_prevᵀ), D, v_prev)</code> (the state <code>S = k_prevᵀ v_prev</code> re-expanded through the carrier). The blocks do not share a state subterm, so there is nothing to bind.</li><li><strong>The block outputs are pairwise distinct modulo the varying integers.</strong> Independent check: canonicalising every block modulo <code>(index, t, offset, sign)</code> leaves <strong>7 distinct</strong> blocks (and distinct even modulo <em>all</em> subterms shared with another block). So no constant-parameter abstraction can collapse them.</li></ol><p>The presentation&#39;s whole advantage — a <em>single shared</em> <code>step</code> — is exactly what the flat DAG erased, and the erasure is <strong>not only the index</strong>: it is the index, the chunk size, and the cross-term spelling at once. Removing the index (this task) is necessary but not sufficient.</p><h2 id="what-it-does-and-does-not-prove" tabindex="-1">What it does and does not prove <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-it-does-and-does-not-prove" aria-label="Permalink to “What it does and does not prove”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Does prove:</strong></p><ul><li>The abstraction the last retro named <strong>exists and is expressible in the existing vocabulary</strong> — a parameter is a wire; <code>split</code>/<code>Arr</code>/<code>Leaf</code>/ <code>Loop</code> suffice, no new node kind. On a regular fold it collapses the blocks, round-trips, and the closure reaches a <code>Loop</code>.</li><li>On the real gate-3 export the blocks <strong>do not</strong> collapse, and the move names <em>why</em>: the cross-term spelling (plus the uneven chunking). So gate 3 is still FAIL, for a reason strictly deeper than &quot;the rule was too narrow&quot;.</li><li>Therefore <strong>the bridge is a presentation, not a search space</strong> — the ADR&#39;s own FAIL branch, now with the missing structure measured.</li></ul><p><strong>Does not prove:</strong></p><ul><li>That <em>no</em> move could ever work — only that abstraction over the <strong>index</strong> cannot, and that the remaining gap is the <em>state spelling</em> (two spellings extraction mixed) plus the <em>chunking</em> (two sizes). A move that also normalises the state spelling is not ruled out; it is named here as the next piece.</li><li>Anything about a <code>catopt-kernel</code> on other grounds. It rules out one justification — &quot;the presentation is a discovery substrate&quot; — again.</li></ul><h2 id="honest-limitation-of-the-move" tabindex="-1">Honest limitation of the move <a class="header-anchor" href="#honest-limitation-of-the-move" aria-label="Permalink to “Honest limitation of the move”">​</a></h2><p>The state is identified structurally (&quot;the outermost subterm that carries none of the block&#39;s own splits&quot;). That is right when the block reads the state <em>through</em> an own-dependent node — which a real attention step does (the state is read via a query, <code>q̃ @ S</code>) — and it is right when the state update lives inside the block. It is <strong>not</strong> right when the block reads the state <em>linearly</em> (<code>o_i = c·S_{i-1} + b_i</code>): there the block-local transform <code>c·S_{i-1}</code> is the largest own-split-free subterm, the templates still agree, and the fold does not reproduce. The move detects this (<code>roundtrip</code> False → <code>verdict=irregular</code>, with a note) rather than mis-folding it, and the limitation is a named residual, not a silent one. A complete move would need the step&#39;s <em>arity</em> (which inputs are state), which the DAG does not carry.</p><h2 id="consequence-for-adr-0009-stage-4" tabindex="-1">Consequence for ADR 0009 stage 4 <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequence-for-adr-0009-stage-4" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequence for ADR 0009 stage 4”">​</a></h2><p>Unchanged and strengthened. Stage 4 was gated on gate 3; gate 3 is still negative, and this task shows the missing piece is <strong>larger</strong> than the previous retro implied: not &quot;a form-level proposer&quot; but a move that normalises the state spelling <em>and</em> the chunking, on top of abstracting the index. Stage 4 still rests on something else or on nothing.</p><h2 id="cost" tabindex="-1">Cost <a class="header-anchor" href="#cost" aria-label="Permalink to “Cost”">​</a></h2><ul><li>~40 s wall for the full <code>--gate2 --extracted --propose-loop --abstract-index</code> run (gate 2 verify + one 15–16 s staged saturation + both gate-3 arms); peak RSS well under 1 GB.</li><li>The abstraction itself is trivial on the winner (7 blocks; the family check is sub-second) and on the control (4–8 blocks).</li><li>New surface: one lab module (~660 lines), one test file (13 tests), ~35 lines of probe wiring. No shipped-package change, no law-bank change, no <code>catopt_core.ir</code> node kind.</li></ul><h2 id="gates-run" tabindex="-1">Gates run <a class="header-anchor" href="#gates-run" aria-label="Permalink to “Gates run”">​</a></h2><p><code>.venv/bin/ruff check</code> + <code>ruff format --check</code> (clean), <code>.venv/bin/ty check</code> (clean), <code>.venv/bin/vulture</code> (clean), <code>.venv/bin/lint-imports</code> (4 kept, 0 broken), <code>scripts/radon_ratchet.py</code> (ok), and <code>pytest tests/test_index_abstract.py tests/test_loop_propose.py tests/test_combinator_bridge.py</code> (35 passed). The full suite was <strong>not</strong> run (memory/time budget; no shipped-package change).</p>`,38)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};